/Title (Retail companies must maintain enough inventory to satisfy customer demand without holding excessive stock. If demand is underestimated, stock-outs and lost sales may occur. If demand is overestimated, the company may carry unnecessary inventory, increasing holding and storage costs. Demand forecasting therefore acts as an important decision-support component in inventory and supply-chain management.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 585 0 R
/Next 725 0 R
>>
