/Title (This report is structured to address the Q39 requirements: industry problem understanding, engineering concept application, solution design, implementation challenges, computational complexity and interpretation in supply- chain optimization. The assignment asks the student to analyze how Dynamic Programming can model demand prediction while considering seasonal trends and data variability.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 646 0 R
/Prev 804 0 R
>>
endobj
725 0 obj
<<
/Title (The selected problem is Retail Demand Forecasting Optimization using Dynamic Programming. The assignment specifically requires consideration of seasonal trends and data variability, followed by a forecasting design, implementation discussion, computational-complexity evaluation and interpretation in supply-chain optimization.)
